0..76 Comment "// Transport in a family over a point and a path to it from a fixed one, the"
77..154 Comment "// motive of based path induction (the HoTT book\'s § 1.12.1): at reflexivity"
155..229 Comment "// it computes to the element given, it reverses a path when the family is"
230..306 Comment "// the paths back, and it refuses a family not over the path\'s own endpoints"
307..336 Comment "// or one that reads no path."
338..359 Comment "// The free naturals."
